# Claim C1 (use-cases 06/09/10): a relative reference inside a pack
# template resolves per generated child ONLY when it is a bare value or
# a meet operand (b: .a and b: .a & integer both work). The moment it
# is an operand of + or a call argument (upper(.a)) it resolves at the
# template's own internal location instead — the NaN path segment —
# contradicting reference-language.md "Generating children": "key() and
# relative references inside the template answer for the child rather
# than for the call".
# expected: {"deploy":{"web":{"a":1,"b":2}}} exit 0
# actual:   exit 1, [aontu/no_path] Cannot resolve value at path
#           $.deploy.NaN.b / Cannot resolve value: .a
names: [web]
deploy: pack($.names, { a: 1, b: .a + 1 })
